I am in the bus.
I find a seat.
I sit there.
I see the conductor.
I signal him.
He comes near me.
"Dada, give me one ticket," I say.
"Where do you need to go?" he asks.
"I need to get to the main metro station," I say.
"I need to alight there."
"Madam, the ticket is twenty rupees," he says.
I take out money from my bag.
I have change.
I give him twenty rupees.
He prints a paper ticket from the machine.
"Here is your ticket," he says.
I take that small ticket.
I put that ticket in my pocket.
Now I sit comfortably.
Travelling by bus is very easy.
